SUMMARY:Chloe Radcliffe Returns to The Comedy Attic
LOCATION:The Comedy Attic\, 123 S Walnut Street\, Bloomington
DESCRIPTION:Hailing from the Midwest and proud of it\, standup and actor Ch
 loe Radcliffe can be seen in Bradley Cooper’s latest film  Is This Thing
  On?  She was named a  Just For Laughs 2025 New Face \, along with one of
   Deadline’s 15 Comedians Ready To Break Out In 2025 \, and one of  Vul
 ture’s Comedians You Should And Will Know . So…get to knowin’ her\, f
 or chrissakes!\n\nA daredevil cyclist in NYC\, Chloe hosts  In Tandem with
  Chloe Radcliffe \, where she interviews other comedians while they ride a 
 tandem bike together. Think Comedians in Cars\, but sweatier.\n\nChloe’s 
 one-woman show  CHEAT \, about her history of infidelity\, led The New Yor
 k Times’ recommendations for the New York Comedy Festival. She sold out 
 her full-month run at the 2023 Edinburgh Fringe Festival\, with reviews cal
 ling it\, “Hilarious and sharply-crafted” (Deadline)\, “Worthy of the
  greats like Mike Birbiglia” (Chortle)\, and “A new take on an old topi
 c\, with hard-hitting punchlines” (The New York Times). Chloe is currentl
 y developing CHEAT for tv.\n\nChloe starred in  Steven Soderbergh’s COMM
 AND Z \, and was nominated for a  2024 WGA award  for her writing on the 
 series. She has been seen on  Comedy Central \,  Don’t Tell Comedy \, a
 nd  After Midnight with Taylor Tomlinson . She was a staff writer on  The
  Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon \, has a comedy feature in development wit
 h Sony\, and was named a  TBS Comic To Watch at the New York Comedy Festi
 val.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/chloe-radcliffe
 -returns-to-the-comedy-attic-20421/
